  "summary": "Berwyn Mayor Robert J. Lovero issued an executive order on Sept. 22, 2026 suspending the city police department's use of Flock license plate reader cameras and barring city employees from accessing Flock data through June 2028, when the city's five-year contract ends. The article notes Berwyn's internal audit found no misuse, references Oak Park's 2025 cancellation, and reports Riverside is weighing renewal of its two-camera Flock contract.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Mayor Robert J. Lovero of Berwyn issued an executive order this week calling for the suspension of the city police's use of Flock cameras and the prohibition of city employees accessing the network of stored Flock data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "the executive order does not cancel the Flock contract or call for the covering, deactivation or removal of the cameras themselves",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "In August 2025, Oak Park's village board voted 4-3 to cancel the village's contract with Flock and shut down its eight license plate reading cameras the next day.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
